# OpsConsole — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values you need.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# NOTHING here is required to boot: with no key the app still runs end to end and
# every check safely returns UNCERTAIN (design principle #1). A key is only
# needed for the AI observation / find steps to actually look at photos.
#
# The Gemini key can ALSO be set at runtime from the in-app Settings page, which
# writes it to data/config.json (git-ignored). The config file wins over these
# env vars when both are present. NEVER commit a real key.

# --- AI (Google Gemini) ---------------------------------------------------
# Your Google AI Studio / Gemini API key. GOOGLE_API_KEY is accepted as an alias.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Vision model used for the observe + find steps. Optional — defaults to
# gemini-2.5-flash. Common choices: gemini-flash-latest, gemini-flash-lite-latest,
# gemini-pro-latest, gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-2.5-flash.
# PREP_VISION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Storage backend ------------------------------------------------------
# Force the evidence/catalog store. Leave unset to auto-detect: "cloudflare" on
# the Workers runtime, "file" (local data/ directory) on plain `next dev`.
# Values: file | cloudflare
# OPSCONSOLE_STORE=

# --- Build (advanced) -----------------------------------------------------
# Override Next.js build output dir (used by the OpenNext/Cloudflare build).
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare deployment note:
# D1 / R2 / KV are supplied to the Worker as BINDINGS (see wrangler.jsonc), not
# as env vars here. Set the production Gemini key as a Worker secret instead:
#   wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
